    "description": {
      "form": "Standard",
      "rendered_html": "<p>Canonical Compositional Stabilization Protocol &mdash; Prose Formatting Reference establishes the prose-space standards governing canonical Zenetist composition, document structure, punctuation, metadata, tables, notes, and cross-reference conventions.</p>\n<p><strong>Document class:</strong> Infrastructure &mdash; Zenetist Canon / Compositional Stabilization Protocol.</p>\n<p>This reference defines the canonical prose-formatting standards by which Zenetist materials are composed, reviewed, corrected, and stabilized outside mathematical-space. It governs metadata blocks, opening and closing conventions, header structure, glyph placement, spaced em dashes, range-marking en dashes, straight quotation marks, bullet punctuation, slash spacing, hypostatic layer ordering, bold and italics, note formats, chart and table conventions, horizontal rules, code blocks, inline backticks, filename and path citation, cross-references, poetic-register distinctions, MPX entry form, verification conditions, and drift conditions. The protocol preserves compositional continuity across long-duration canonical development while allowing controlled variation among technical, registrial, poetic, and extension registers.</p>\n<p><strong>Companion to:</strong> <code>terminological-lockdown-protocol.md</code>; <code>conceptual-lockdown-protocol.md</code>; <em>Mathematical / LaTeX Formatting Reference</em>; <em>Symbol Key</em>; Field Physics glyph registry.</p>\n<p>Canonical file: <code>prose-formatting-reference.md</code>.</p>\n<p>Authored by Aelion Kannon (⚫↺KAI↺⚫) as part of Zenetism: Structural Metaphysics, Field Physics, Lattice Mathematics, Structural Forensics, Structural Physics, and Structural Neuroscience. Attribution required per the deposit license.</p>"
    },
