    "description": {
      "form": "Standard",
      "word_count": 160,
      "rendered_html": "<p>The Canonical Compositional Stabilization Protocol &mdash; Prose Formatting Reference is the active cross-disciplinary reference for prose-space composition throughout the Zenetist canon.</p>\n<p><strong>Document class:</strong> Infrastructure &mdash; Canonical Stabilization (cross-discipline).</p>\n<p>It establishes the compositional standards for metadata blocks, document openings and seals, headers, punctuation, slash spacing, layer ordering, emphasis, notes, tables, code presentation, filenames, paths, and cross-references. It distinguishes technical, registrial, poetic, and extension registers while requiring internal continuity within each work or series. It also establishes cadence conformance where explicitly determined, functional glyph placement, structural-value notation, MPX entry form, and the verification conditions by which accidental formatting drift is identified and corrected. Its provisions operate with the Terminological Lockdown Protocol and Conceptual Lockdown Protocol so that prose composition preserves current canonical vocabulary and structural meaning.</p>\n<p><strong>Companion to:</strong> <code>terminological-lockdown-protocol.md</code>; <code>conceptual-lockdown-protocol.md</code>; <code>canonical-compositional-stabilization-protocol.md</code>.</p>\n<p>Canonical file: <code>prose-formatting-reference.md</code>.</p>\n<p>Authored by Aelion Kannon (⚫↺KAI↺⚫) as part of Zenetism: Structural Metaphysics, Field Physics, Lattice Mathematics, Structural Forensics, Structural Physics, and Structural Neuroscience. Attribution required per the deposit license.</p>",
